  "articleBody": "Installing baseboards can seem straightforward, but there are a few common mistakes that can really mess up your finished look. First off, inaccurate measurements are a huge culprit. Cutting pieces too short is a big no-no because you can't add material back! Always measure each wall section precisely and double-check before making your cut. Another frequent error is poor corner joints. Whether you're coping or mitering, those corners need to be tight and flush, otherwise, you'll end up with visible gaps. Nailing into drywall instead of studs is another big one; your baseboards won't be securely fastened and could pull away over time. Take the time to find those studs and nail directly into them. And while caulk is great for finishing, don't rely on it to hide major fit problems. If you've got big gaps because of uneven walls or bad cuts, caulk will only draw attention to them. Acclimating your baseboards to the room for a day or two before installation is also super important; it helps prevent warping after they're installed. When you're dealing with a whole house or intricate designs, or if your walls and floors aren't perfectly straight, these mistakes can become incredibly frustrating. Sometimes, calling in a seasoned pro like HH Remodeling LLC just saves you a lot of headache and ensures a really polished result. We get it right, every time.",
